  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.49,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.04,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.48 from 5 h onward, which could mean the reader was saturating. I diluted the 18 h aliquot and rescaled the readings by the dilution factor. If the reader were saturating, these would come out higher than the undiluted reading.\n\n| Dilution | Reading(s) | Rescaled OD |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 (undiluted) | 0.4885 | 0.489 |\n| 2 (2 replicates) | 0.245, 0.244 | 0.489 |\n| 3 (1 replicate, 2 runs) | 0.176 and 0.166 | 0.528 and 0.498 |\n| 10 (2 replicates) | 0.049, 0.047 | 0.481 |\n\nThe rescaled values stay between 0.48 and 0.53 and do not rise with dilution. The first 3x reading (0.528) was somewhat high, but a repeat gave 0.498, so I treat it as noise. The plateau therefore looks like a real stationary phase at an OD of about 0.49, and the undiluted readings are not under-reporting biomass."
  },
